":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.5.beta3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 22621) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7652) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-8700K CPU @ 3.70GHz (12 threads) - 31.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nTrying to use a sampler3D texture with `hint_default_transparent`  does absolutely nothing to the alpha channel.\n\nLooking at the code, you can see that they all fall back to a WHITE texture (except samplercubearray which falls back to black?)\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2a9ff392645f1e1e073d937f1f6fb8feac896b2f/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/material_storage.cpp#L1002-L1016\n\nIf these hint types are not supported by these sampler types, you'd expect them to throw an error at the shader compiler.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake a ShaderMaterial, and add a uniform sampler3D with hint_type_transparent then don't set a texture in the inspector.\nIn the fragment shader, sample the texture and output the alpha channel to e.g. EMISSION\n`EMISSION = vec3(texture(volume_texture, vec3(0.0f)).a);`\nYou will obviously see that the material lights up, even though the alpha channel is supposed to be 0\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A. ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","s